Earth
=====

Earth is a movable, resizable Motif globe demonstration. In modern-light and
modern-dark profiles it projects one 2048x1024 world texture onto a sphere,
with bilinear sampling, lighting and an antialiased silhouette. Classic and
high-contrast profiles retain the original two-color artwork. The canvas is
black in every profile, and the globe stays centered and uniformly scaled.

Right-click the globe to show the speed slider below it, within the same
window. Right-click again to hide it and reclaim the space. There is no popup.
Only the globe area is black; the slider uses normal theme colors and a
scale-aware 32-pixel track height, with its preferred overall height allocated.

Left-click without dragging stops the globe. Hold and drag left/right to turn
it directly; release to continue at the gesture's direction and speed, bounded
to +/-20 RPM. Holding still for 150 ms before release stops it. Rotation is
frozen immediately on press, with no automatic timer movement during a drag.
Scroll up to enlarge the globe or down to shrink it in fine 2% steps (5%–200%). The zoom
center is always the center of the globe area, even in a non-square window.
The slider reflects the released speed. Escape cancels a drag. Releasing
outside the window still ends the drag because the pointer is grabbed.

Animation uses one cancellable Xt timer with a default cadence of 30 FPS.
Rotation is computed from monotonic elapsed time, independently of FPS. Missed
presentation deadlines are skipped; there is no catch-up burst. The default
speed is 0.5 RPM, one revolution every two minutes. The slider displays RPM
from -20.0 to 20.0 in 0.1 increments. Zero pauses; negative values reverse.

Resources and options:
  speed / -speed N  Integer tenths of RPM, -200..200; default 5 (0.5 RPM).
  fps / -fps N      Presentation rate, 1..120; default 30.
Out-of-range resource values are clamped. Pausing removes the timer entirely.
The foreground/background resources set classic land/water colors.

Examples:
  earth -xrm 'ckCoreMotif.appearanceProfile: modern-light'
  earth -xrm 'ckCoreMotif.appearanceProfile: modern-dark' -fps 60 -speed 3

The installed world-map.xpm is loaded once through the toolkit's XPM loader;
no JPEG/PNG decoder or network is needed. A build-tree source-path fallback
supports running before installation. Modern rendering requires TrueColor.
See MAP-LICENSE for NASA source, attribution and conversion details.
